Powered by FUTO Swipe

This keyboard includes models from futo-org/futo-swipe, licensed under the
FUTO Model Weights License 1.0, not GPL. The complete model license is installed
at /usr/share/swipe-keyboard/models/FUTO-MODEL-LICENSE.md. Model revision,
immutable download URLs and SHA-256 checksums are recorded in assets.lock.json.

Keyboard source: https://github.com/itsdestin/swipe-keyboard (GPL-3.0-or-later;
see LICENSE). Recursive source dependency revisions and local modifications
are recorded in SOURCE-PROVENANCE.txt in the corresponding source archive.
The source archive is a required companion to binary build artifacts; these
recipes do not publish anything.

FUTO swipe-library and its recursively included ExecuTorch dependencies carry
their own licenses/notices. Their source files and notices are included in the
companion source archive; installed third-party notices are collected at build
time. ExecuTorch is BSD-3-Clause; see the corresponding upstream LICENSE.

English dictionary is generated from Android LatinIME/AOSP word lists
(Apache-2.0, original notices retained) and wordfreq 3.1.1 English frequency
data (CC-BY-SA-4.0). Transformation: scripts/dict/wordfreq_combined.py combines
entries, preserves AOSP frequencies, adjusts apostrophe pairs, and filters
likely misspellings, with a 250000-entry cap. The resulting combined dictionary
is distributed under CC-BY-SA-4.0 with attribution to AOSP contributors and
Robyn Speer/wordfreq contributors. Original input URLs/revisions/checksums
are in assets.lock.json; wordfreq source and attribution/license information:
https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq and https://pypi.org/project/wordfreq/3.1.1/.
The Spanish, French and German next-word n-gram models are compact baseline models trained from the pinned Tatoeba sentence exports, not foreign FUTO neural weights. Tatoeba's text uses CC BY 2.0 France; retain each language pack's full contributor list and attribution notice. The Tatoeba notice is installed beside the package license at `share/licenses/swipe-keyboard/TATOEBA-CC-BY-2.0-FR.txt` (normally `/usr/share/licenses/...` or `/app/share/licenses/...`). Spanish Spain and Mexico share one Spanish model; model/data hashes and provenance are in assets.lock.json and packaging/language-models/README.md. This is a small general Spanish/French/German baseline and makes no region-specific Spanish or Gboard-parity claim.

Contextual prediction is language-specific; an unavailable or corrupt pack never falls back to English. Current-word completion uses the selected profile's own dictionary; next-word suggestions use that profile's model when available. On stock Plasma, next-word model input is limited to words this keyboard confirmed in the current field because raw application completion preferences are not fully exposed. Sensitive and restricted fields remain blocked. The bundled Deck backend retains its raw-policy bridge and stricter application vetoes.

Optional evaluation data and neural reranking models are not included.
